    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but you said \"not a permanent solution\"... i'm not talking about letting go of baggage. i mean a total system exit. if a program is fundamentally corrupted and just keeps crashing the environment, the most logical thing for the admin to do is to terminate the process completely. to wipe the instance. wouldn't it be more efficient to just end the execution once it stops being productive?",
